{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"19. The Just","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp256-272'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 256–272 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Dhammaṭṭhavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>19. The Just </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The “Established in Dhamma” Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp256'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vinicchayamahāmattavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tena hoti dhammaṭṭho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You don’t become just </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not established in Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yenatthaṁ sāhasā naye; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by passing hasty judgment. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>if one seeks benefit using violence; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca atthaṁ anatthañca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>An astute person evaluates both </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a wise person does not wish to have </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ubho niccheyya paṇḍito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>what is pertinent and what is irrelevant. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>both benefit and detriment. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp257'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Asāhasena dhammena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A wise one judges others without haste, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who guides others nonviolently, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samena nayatī pare; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>justly and impartially; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>peacefully, in accordance with Dhamma, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhammassa gutto medhāvī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that guardian of the law </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>such a wise person is a guardian of the Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“dhammaṭṭho”ti pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be just. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and is said to be established in Dhamma. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp258'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Chabbaggiyavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tena paṇḍito hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You’re not an astute scholar </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not wise </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yāvatā bahu bhāsati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>just because you speak a lot. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>just because one talks a lot. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khemī averī abhayo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who is secure, free of enmity and fear, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who is safe, non-hostile, harmless and fearless </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“paṇḍito”ti pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be astute. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be wise. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp259'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ekudānakhīṇāsavavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tāvatā dhammadharo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You’re not one who has memorized the teaching </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not an upholder of the Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yāvatā bahu bhāsati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>just because you recite a lot. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>just because one talks a lot. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca appampi sutvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Someone who directly sees the teaching </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Even if one has learned little </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhammaṁ kāyena passati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>after hearing only a little </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>but personally sees the Dhamma, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa ve dhammadharo hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is truly one who has memorized the teaching, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>then one is an upholder of the Dhamma, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yo dhammaṁ nappamajjati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for they can never forget it. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who does not neglect the Dhamma. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp260'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Lakuṇḍakabhaddiyattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tena thero so hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You don’t become a senior </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not an elder </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yenassa palitaṁ siro; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by getting some grey hairs; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>just because one has grey hairs on one's head. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paripakko vayo tassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for one ripe only in age, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is who is decrepit and feeble </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“moghajiṇṇo”ti vuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to have aged in vain. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be an old fool. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp261'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yamhi saccañca dhammo ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who is truthful and principled, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>But one who is truthful, in accordance with the Dhamma, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ahiṁsā saṁyamo damo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>harmless, restrained, and self-controlled, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>harmless, self-restrained, trained, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa ve vantamalo dhīro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>attentive, purged of stains, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>steadfast, and free of all contaminants </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“thero” iti pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be a senior. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be an elder. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp262'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sambahulabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na vākkaraṇamattena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Not by mere enunciation, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Not by the quality of their conversation </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vaṇṇapokkharatāya vā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or a beautiful complexion </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or the beauty of their appearance </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sādhurūpo naro hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>does a person become holy, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is a person considered excellent, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>issukī maccharī saṭho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>if they’re jealous, stingy, and devious. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>if they are envious, stingy, and deceitful. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp263'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yassa cetaṁ samucchinnaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But if they’ve cut that out, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has shredded, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mūlaghaccaṁ samūhataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>dug it up at the root, eradicated it, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>uprooted, and destroyed those qualities, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa vantadoso medhāvī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that intelligent one, purged of vice, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a wise person who has expelled their defects, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“sādhurūpo”ti vuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be holy. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be excellent. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp264'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Hatthakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na muṇḍakena samaṇo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A liar and breaker of vows is no ascetic </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not a contemplative just because one has a shaven head. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>abbato alikaṁ bhaṇaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>just because they shave their head. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>If one has no religious practices, tells lies, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Icchālobhasamāpanno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>How on earth can one be an ascetic </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and is full of desire and greed, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samaṇo kiṁ bhavissati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who’s full of desire and greed? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>how can they be a contemplative? </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp265'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca sameti pāpāni, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who stops all wicked deeds, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who tranquilizes all that is evil, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aṇuṁthūlāni sabbaso; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>great and small, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>whether minor or major, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Samitattā hi pāpānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>because of stopping wicked deeds </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who has tranquilized all that is evil </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“samaṇo”ti pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be an ascetic. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be a contemplative. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp266'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarabrāhmaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tena bhikkhu so hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You don’t become a mendicant </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not a monk </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yāvatā bhikkhate pare; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>just by begging from others. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>just because one receives almsfood from others. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vissaṁ dhammaṁ samādāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who has undertaken domestic duties </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who takes up a flawed doctrine </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhikkhu hoti na tāvatā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has not yet become a mendicant. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is not a monk. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp267'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yodha puññañca pāpañca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But one living a spiritual life, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has discarded both merit and evil, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bāhetvā brahmacariyavā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who has banished both merit and evil, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>lives a spiritual life, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅkhāya loke carati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who wanders having appraised the world, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and wanders in the world with careful consideration </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sa ve “bhikkhū”ti vuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be a mendicant. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be a monk. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp268'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Titthiyavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na monena munī hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You don’t become a sage by being sagelike, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not a sage if they act like one </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mūḷharūpo aviddasu; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>while still confused and ignorant. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>yet are confused and ignorant. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca tulaṁva paggayha, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The astute one who holds the scales, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>A wise person who carefully weighs their options, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>varamādāya paṇḍito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>taking only the best, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>chooses the best, </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp269'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pāpāni parivajjeti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and shunning the bad—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and completely avoids evil </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sa munī tena so muni; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that is a sage, <j>and that is how one becomes a sage. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is a sage; because of this one is a sage. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo munāti ubho loke, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who sagely weighs both in the world, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who evaluates both of these in the world </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“muni” tena pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is thereby said to be a sage. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be a sage. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp270'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bālisikavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na tena ariyo hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You don’t become a noble one </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One is not noble </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yena pāṇāni hiṁsati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by harming living beings. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>if one harms living beings. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ahiṁsā sabbapāṇānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One harmless toward all living beings </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who does not harm any living being </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“ariyo”ti pavuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is said to be a noble one. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is said to be noble. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp271'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sambahulasīlādisampannabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na sīlabbatamattena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Not by precepts and observances, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Not just by morality or by spiritual practices </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bāhusaccena vā pana; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor by much learning, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or by learning a lot </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha vā samādhilābhena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor by meditative immersion, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or by gaining concentration </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vivittasayanena vā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor by living in seclusion, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or by sleeping in seclusion </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp272'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Phusāmi nekkhammasukhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>do I experience the bliss of renunciation </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or by experiencing the happiness of renunciation </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aputhujjanasevitaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>not frequented by ordinary people. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or by associating with uncommon people </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhikkhu vissāsamāpādi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A mendicant cannot rest confident </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>should a monk be satisfied </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>appatto āsavakkhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>without attaining the end of defilements. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>as long as one’s defilements have not been eliminated. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Dhammaṭṭhavaggo ekūnavīsatimo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
